agent-cli-rust
==============

A lightweight terminal-based Software Engineering Agent written in Rust.

Project Status
--------------

  This project is under active development.

  Currently available:

  - OpenAI-compatible single-turn chat
  - TOML-based LLM configuration
  - Environment-variable API key fallback
  - HTTP fetch command
  - Minimal Agent Runtime
  - Structured tool calling with a built-in add tool
  - Deterministic unit and CLI integration tests

  The Agent Runtime is not yet connected to the CLI.

  ## Commands

  ### Chat

  cargo run -- chat <CONFIG_PATH> [PROMPT]

  When PROMPT is omitted, input is read from stdin.

  ### Read configuration

  cargo run -- read-config <CONFIG_PATH>

  The command reports whether an API key is configured without printing it.

  ### Fetch

  cargo run -- fetch <URL> [--max-chars N]

  ### Version

  cargo run -- --version

  ## Configuration

  [llm]
  base_url = "https://api.openai.com/v1"
  api_key = ""
  model = "gpt-4.1"
  temperature = 0.7

  src/
  ├── main.rs                 CLI entry and command dispatch
  ├── cli.rs                  CLI definitions
  ├── config.rs               Configuration loading and validation
  ├── agent.rs                Agent execution loop
  ├── tools.rs                Built-in tool execution
  ├── openai_compatible.rs    OpenAI-compatible protocol integration
  └── commands/               User-facing CLI commands
